# Scheduled jobs for the household ledger (Raspberry Pi / any Linux box).
#
#   crontab -e        # as the same user the service runs as, `pi`
#
# Then paste the four lines below the comments. Check they took with
# `crontab -l`, and watch them run with `journalctl -t expenses -f` — every job
# logs through `logger` so a failure at 04:00 leaves something to read at 09:00
# rather than nothing at all.
#
# Why these run from cron and not from inside the app: nothing may touch the
# network during a request (invariant 7). `fetch-rates` and `check-limits` are
# the only two things in the codebase that open a socket, and this file is the
# only thing that calls them.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
APP=/home/pi/expenses
FLASK=/home/pi/expenses/.venv/bin/flask

# --- exchange rates, daily at 04:10 ---------------------------------------
#
# Runs daily; refreshes only when the cache is older than FX_MAX_AGE_DAYS, so
# the provider sees roughly one call a week and a day the Pi was off is caught
# up by the next morning rather than skipped.
#
# This one matters more than it looks. `transactions.py` refuses a
# cross-currency transfer whose two sides disagree by more than a factor of ten,
# and it does that by comparing against the cached rate. An empty cache has
# nothing to compare against, so the guard stays silent — it is only as awake as
# this line.
10 4 * * * cd $APP && $FLASK --app app fetch-rates 2>&1 | logger -t expenses

# --- budget warnings, hourly ----------------------------------------------
#
# Sends at most one message per budget per threshold per period, so hourly is
# not hourly nagging: crossing 80% at 14:00 is one message, and 15:00 sends
# nothing. Hourly rather than daily because "you have passed the grocery budget"
# is worth knowing before the next shop, not the following morning.
0 * * * * cd $APP && $FLASK --app app check-limits 2>&1 | logger -t expenses

# --- orphaned receipt files, Sundays at 03:30 ------------------------------
#
# Deleting a transaction cascades its attachment rows away; the JPEGs on disk do
# not go with them. A trigger records the debt in `orphaned_files` and this pays
# it. Weekly is fine — the rows are the record, the disk is just late.
30 3 * * 0 cd $APP && $FLASK --app app sweep-uploads 2>&1 | logger -t expenses

# --- backup, nightly at 02:00 ---------------------------------------------
#
# SQLite's online backup API plus a tarball of uploads/, keeping a fortnight.
# Not strictly part of running the app, and the first thing anyone wishes they
# had turned on. If the Pi's SD card is the only copy, there is no copy.
0 2 * * * cd $APP && .venv/bin/python scripts/backup.py --keep 14 2>&1 | logger -t expenses
